From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: record the stack ABI a program is built for

binfmt_wasm refuses a program that does not carry the stack layout
version it runs. crt_arch.h emits the gmux.abi custom section with the
version, which the program's link keeps.
---
 arch/wasm/crt_arch.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/crt_arch.h b/arch/wasm/crt_arch.h
index 48e06fb..2173743 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/crt_arch.h
+++ b/arch/wasm/crt_arch.h
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[], char *envp[])
  * TODO: fix this hack by refactoring musl and moving things into a .S file.
  */
 #ifndef SHARED
+/* the stack ABI binfmt_wasm checks at exec; clang makes a custom section only from asm */
+__asm__(".section .custom_section.gmux.abi,\"\",@\n.int32 1\n");
+
 void _start(void)
 {
 	void _start_c(/* no prototype on purpose */);
-- 
